[38;5;231m⏺[39m [1mDesign — Section 1 of 3: module layout and public API[0m

  [1mNew file [38;5;153msrc/validation.js[0m (ES module). It exports:

  - [38;5;153mvalidate(values, schema)[39m — the only entry point. Pure, synchronous, no DOM.
  - Rule factories: [38;5;153mrequired()[39m, [38;5;153mminLength(n)[39m, [38;5;153mmaxLength(n)[39m, [38;5;153memail()[39m, [38;5;153mpattern(re, message)[39m, [38;5;153mrange(min, max)[39m.

  A rule is just [38;5;153m(value) => string | null[39m. A factory is a function returning one. That's the whole contract — a custom
  rule is any function of that shape, so [38;5;153mpassword: [required(), match(/[0-9]/, "Needs a digit")][39m needs no change to the
  shared file.

  Each factory takes an optional [38;5;153mmessage[39m override as its last argument, so a form can say [38;5;153mrequired("Pick a username")[39m
  without a separate messages layer.

  [1mOne deliberate exception to the rules list:[0m [38;5;153mrequired()[39m short-circuits. If a field is empty and [38;5;153mrequired()[39m is present,
  that's the only error reported for the field — you never see "Required" and "Must be a valid email" at once. If
  [38;5;153mrequired()[39m is absent, an empty value passes every other rule (i.e. optional fields are only checked when filled). This
  is the behavior people expect but rarely write down, so it goes in the spec.

  [1m[38;5;153msrc/validation.js[39m sits next to the existing [38;5;153msrc/[39m files but is unrelated to them.[0m [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m are a
  CommonJS Node island; the new module is ESM for the browser. They don't interact, and I'm not touching them. If you'd
  rather keep the browser code out of [38;5;153msrc/[39m entirely, say so and I'll put it at [38;5;153mvalidation.js[39m in the root next to [38;5;153mapp.js[39m.

  [1mTooling.[0m The project currently has no test runner, no linter, and zero dependencies. Since the whole point of
  "validator only" was testability, I'd add exactly one thing: [1m[38;5;153mnode --test[39m with a [38;5;153mtest/validation.test.js[0m, wired as [38;5;153mnpm
[39m  [38;5;153mtest[39m in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m. It ships with Node, so dependencies stay at zero. I would [3mnot[0m add a linter/formatter or e2e
  infrastructure as part of this task — happy to if you want them, but they're not needed for this change.

  Does Section 1 look right?

